# libabigail suppressions for test/abi/check.sh. See
# test/abi/README.md.
#
# This file is empty on purpose. The ABI dump only contains the public
# headers' types and one pointer for each API function, so there is
# nothing to filter out. The rule that lets sized structs grow at the
# end is generated by check.sh.
#
# Only add a suppression for a reported change that we know is
# compatible, with a comment that explains why. Keep each rule as narrow
# as possible, because a rule hides every change it matches:
#
# - A [suppress_type] rule that matches a type hides all changes to that
#   type, not only the one you meant to allow.
# - libabigail treats struct members as variables, so a
#   [suppress_variable] rule that matches by name can also hide changes
#   to struct members.
#
# After adding a rule, make a change it should not hide and check that
# test/abi/check.sh diff still fails.
